      "content": "Right, let's build your guide from the two questions you actually gave me. Two honesty notes first: your profile's weak-topics list is empty, and the subject line says Mathematics/trigonometry while these excerpts are Afrikaans comprehension questions - so this guide covers the excerpts only, not trig. Also, the passage itself is not in what I can see, so I cannot give you the answers. What I can give you is the method.\n\nQuestion 1 (ex_1): 'Watter gevoel dra Mike se woorde in RAAMPIE 2 oor?' This is a tone/emotion question on a visual text. Method: read Mike's words in RAAMPIE 2, underline the emotive words, name the feeling in one word, then back it up with the exact words from the frame. Think of it like reading the room at a taxi rank - you don't need a speech, you pick up the vibe from a few words and a face.\n\nQuestion 2 (ex_2): 'Hoe sluit prof. Jennifer Thompson se verduideliking van die genetiese manipulasie van rys by die laaste sin van paragraaf 1 aan?' This is a linking question. Method: find the last sentence of paragraaf 1, find the matching idea in Thompson's explanation, and state the link in one sentence - 'Both say X' or 'Her explanation shows how/why X happens.' Like connecting the ingredients list to the final dish at a braai - the explanation is the 'how', the last sentence is the 'what'.\n\nCAPS tip: answer in the language of the question, quote the text, keep it short.",
